course: dictionary
lesson: 6779
title: A word for an eye helper
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An optometrist is a person who tests your eyes. Look at the parts of the word for clues: "optom" is about sight, and "-ist" means a person who does a certain job, like a florist sells flowers. So an optometrist is a person whose job is to check how well you can see.
explain: The sentences tell you more. «An optometrist tests vision with a letter chart whose lines get smaller» shows the job: checking how well you can see. The words «lenses» and «prescription» show that the test can end with glasses or contact lenses.
explain: Use the swap check: put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. «Jo has an eye test at the optometrist on Monday» makes sense when you read it as "a person trained to test eyesight", so you have understood the word.
fact: An optometrist is a person trained to test people's eyesight.
fact: An optometrist checks eye health and can prescribe glasses or contact lenses.
fact: «Optometrist» is a noun, and its plural is optometrists.
fact: «Eye drops can widen the pupils so the optometrist can see inside the eye.»
fact: The blurriness from eye drops wears off after a few hours, and until then bright sun can feel dazzling.
exercise: «An optometrist tests vision with a letter chart whose lines get smaller.» What does an optometrist do? | Drives buses to school | Sells ice cream at the seaside | *Tests how well people can see | Fixes broken roads
exercise: Jo says, «I've got an eye test at the optometrist on Monday.» What is an optometrist? | *A person trained to test eyesight | A type of bright sunshine | A kind of eye drop | A place to buy bread
exercise: «Eye drops can widen the pupils, so bright sun can feel dazzling.» Why might bright sun feel dazzling? | Dazzling means quiet and dark | The sun is hiding behind a cloud | *Wide pupils let in more light | Eye drops close the pupils
test: «An optometrist finds out with letter charts, lights and lenses.» Which tools does an optometrist use? | *Letter charts, lights and lenses | Hammers and saws | Frying pans and spoons
test: Which word means a person trained to test eyesight? | *optometrist | plumber | florist
exam: Ella's new glasses help her see the board. Based on «glasses bend the light a little more or less so the picture lands right», why do glasses help a person see clearly? | *They bend the light so the picture lands right | They stop you from blinking | They change the colour of the sky | They make everything darker
